integer.\n\nNow, note the following regarding the expression $6p+10q+3:$\n\n- All terms, apart from the constant term, have a common factor of $2.$\n\n- The constant term can be written as $3=2+1.$\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{odd}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =6p+10q+3 \\\\  & =(6p+10q+2)+1 \\\\  & =2({{3p+5q+1}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=3p+5q+1\\in Z.$" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407124 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407099 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407124 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407102 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407124 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407112 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407124 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407117 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407124 1069 "q-184062" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407124 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407124 1071 "Suppose $n=4i+2j-8,$ where $i,j\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument." 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407124 1072 #uuid "2f34688d-9a70-5e5f-86f3-8ad4e9bec34c" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407124 1074 "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nNotice that all terms in the expression $4i+2j-8$ have a common factor of $2.$ \n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{even}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =4i+2j-8 \\\\  & =2({{2i+j-4}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=2i+j-4\\in Z.$" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407125 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407098 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407125 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407105 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407125 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407118 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407125 1069 "q-184102" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407125 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407125 1071 "Suppose $n=10m+4,$ where $m\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is even." 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407125 1072 #uuid "45d8a589-5d18-5ea9-a082-e4a7691a3a49" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407125 1074 "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is even since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =10m+4 \\\\  & =2({{5m+2}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=5m+2,$ which is an integer." 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407126 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407101 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407126 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407115 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407126 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407119 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407126 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407121 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407126 1069 "q-184080" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407126 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407126 1071 "Suppose $n=6{m}^{5}+8{m}^{4}-1,$ where $m\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument." 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407126 1072 #uuid "56052108-5098-50da-941c-873f362e867d" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407126 1074 "An integer is *odd* if it can be written as $2a+1,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nNow, note the following regarding the expression $6{m}^{5}+8{m}^{4}-1:$\n\n- All terms, apart from the constant term, have a common factor of $2.$\n\n- The constant term can be written as $-1=-2+1.$\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{odd}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =6{m}^{5}+8{m}^{4}-1 \\\\  & =(6{m}^{5}+8{m}^{4}-2)+1 \\\\  & =2({{3{m}^{5}+4{m}^{4}-1}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=3{m}^{5}+4{m}^{4}-1$ is an integer." 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592