s:\n\nThe number $n$ is odd since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =-10q-5 \\\\  & =(-10b-6)+1 \\\\  & =2({{-5b-3}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=-5b-3,$ which is an integer." 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407129 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407106 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407129 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407108 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407129 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407113 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407129 1069 "q-184128" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407129 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407129 1071 "Suppose $n=1-8p,$ where $p\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is odd." 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407129 1072 #uuid "89ca628f-f5b6-5773-9b1c-0f25806d7d8c" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407129 1074 "An integer is *odd* if it can be written as $2a+1,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is odd since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =1-8p \\\\  & =(-8p)+1 \\\\  & =2({{-4p}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=-4p,$ which is an integer." 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407130 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407095 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407130 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407096 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407130 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407114 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407130 1069 "q-184120" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407130 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407130 1071 "Suppose $n=-10-30q,$ where $q\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is even." 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407130 1072 #uuid "988b9965-fc57-5a1f-a7d2-bc319da35474" 13194139533529 17592186045585 true] [17592186407130 1074 "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$